from common import *
it('KERNEL-0082','mechanism','3.2','(9) Frame growth at an epoch (item 81 (b); J-A81.31): a frame only grows, and only where §4.11 grows it at an epoch; the new frame is the (9) rule at the epoch population target, taken at most at the cap (as §1.1 clamps a request), at the frame own aspect, centred on (0, 0), so it encloses its predecessor; the range bound holds for every grown coordinate. The growth runs as §3.3 declared sequence of single-level batches sharing one clear region, each with rederivesFrom S1.',['§3.2 (9) Frame growth'],'kernel (trigger owned by §4.11 / V06 evolution)',['§4.11 epoch grow path','@frameRule','§1.1 cap clamp','@declaredSequence','@clearRegion'],['§2.2 Plat.frame','§4.11','V06 evolution epochs','§7.4 epoch undo'],['frameGrowth','item 81 (b)','J-A81.31'])
it('KERNEL-0083','term','3.2','Defined term LAPSING STRETCH: a stretch of the old margin ring or of the old border rectangle that carries no other row of its chain level or a coarser one.',['§3.2 (9) Frame growth'],'kernel',['@StretchRef','§2.2 rows'],['@frameGrowth steps (b), (c)'],['lapsing stretch'])
it('KERNEL-0084','term','3.2','Defined term REGION (of a frame growth): the union of the L1 faces beside a lapsing stretch and those the new frame rectangle will cross - whole L1 faces, as a carve footprint is (§3.3).',['§3.2 (9) Frame growth'],'kernel',['@clearRegion'],['@frameGrowth step (a)'],['region'])
it('KERNEL-0085','step','3.2','Frame growth (a) Clearing (L1): one L1 batch removes the content finer than L1 of every face of the region (§3.3 rule 1); a locked or pinned owner returns as a conflict (F-EDIT, §5.2), so no deletion of the committed growth joins two faces finer than L1 and its new rectangle crosses none.',['§3.2 (9) (a)'],'kernel',['@clearRegion','@E_LOCKED'],['@frameGrowth (b), (c)','F-EDIT §5.2'],['frame growth clearing'])
it('KERNEL-0086','step','3.2','Frame growth (b) The margin (L0): one L0 batch inserts the new outer ring as the margin chain, then S1 water faces in the band between old and new ring (§4.11), then strips the old ring margin rows by removeEdges on two StretchRefs that together cover it (§3.4). A stretch left with no row is deleted, joining the faces either side (land with land, water with water, each cleared L1 face beside it with the ring one); a stretch that keeps a row keeps its edge, re-levelled by §2.2 rule 3 (a) (as where S1 lays a shore along it). Plat.frame takes the new frame as this batch commits.',['§3.2 (9) (b)'],'kernel',['@removeEdges','@StretchRef','§4.1 S1 water','§2.2 rule 3 (a)'],['§2.2 Plat.frame','@frameGrowth (c)'],['frame growth margin'])
it('KERNEL-0087','step','3.2','Frame growth (c) The border (L1): one L1 batch inserts the new frame rectangle as the border chain by §3.6 insertion (a way it crosses sharing the crossing vertex) and strips the old rectangle border rows alike; a stretch that also carries another L1 row - the settlement perimeter or a reservation boundary running along the frame (§2.2 rule 1) - stays.',['§3.2 (9) (c)'],'kernel',['@insertChain','@removeEdges'],['§4.11 continuation of ways'],['frame growth border'])
it('KERNEL-0088','rule','3.2','Frame growth: a vertex of an old chain that keeps a row or another edge stays (a through-road end on the old ring is an antenna end until §4.11 continues its way); every other vertex dissolves or stays by §2.2 rule 3.',['§3.2 (9) after (c)'],'kernel',['§2.2 rule 3'],['§4.11 way continuation'],['antenna end'])
it('KERNEL-0089','rule','3.2','Frame growth of underground parts: every underground part (its outer ring the frame with its margin - the sewer II.7.2, each further part §2.2 rule 1) grows by (a) and (b) on its own key, the margin rows of its own record (§2.2 rule 1) instead of the Terrain ones, with no water and no border.',['§3.2 (9) after (c)'],'kernel (parts owned by §2.2 / II.7 / V04 underground)',['§2.2 rule 1 parts','II.7.2 sewer part'],['V04 underground','II.7 sewer layer'],['underground part growth'])
it('KERNEL-0090','rule','3.2','Frame growth of rasters: each §2.3 raster extends by whole cells on each side until it covers the grown arena, keeping its cellCm and cell alignment, so every old cell keeps its place and every stored height its value; S1 fills the new cells; the hydro fields (flow direction, flat rank, accumulation) are recomputed over the grown grid by the §2.3 mechanism (an old edge cell gains neighbours and the ring may drain inward), every river traced course inside the old arena unchanged.',['§3.2 (9) after (c)','§2.3 (line ~882 resolution kept when an epoch grows)'],'kernel / §2.3 model (raster record)',['§2.3 rasters','§2.3 hydro mechanism','§4.1 S1'],['§4 hydrology consumers','§8 terrain render'],['raster extension','hydro'])
it('KERNEL-0091','rule','3.2','Frame growth: what changes is the region faces, the faces beside a deleted stretch and the ring new faces, at each level that sees them - §4.11 stages continue the ways and re-derive them; every other face keeps its ring, owner and nested faces (re-parented where its parent was joined, §3.3).',['§3.2 (9) after (c)'],'kernel',['@frameGrowth'],['§4.11 re-derivation','@reparent'],['least-disruption frame growth'])
it('KERNEL-0092','rule','3.2','Frame growth draws no random stream in the kernel part, so a replay of the log re-grows the frame byte for byte; where §7.4 allows an epoch undo, its undo record restores the old frame and what the three batches removed.',['§3.2 (9) after (c)'],'kernel (undo rows owned by §7.4)',['§6 log replay','§7.4 lifecycle'],['§7.4 epoch undo','§6 replay'],['frame growth undo','replay'])
it('KERNEL-0093','fallback','3.2','Pre-decided fallback: if M4 memory measurement of the extreme growth - a TOWN grown in one epoch to the cap, whose kept 5 m heights over the cap arena are about 15.7 M cells (about 63 MB; a METROPOLIS made at the cap holds about 3.9 M) - exceeds the §12.8 METROPOLIS line, a growth that changes the rung re-grids each raster at the new rung cellCm (heights by the sampler bilinear read of the old grid, flow fields recomputed, every standing entity keeping its stored baseCm), and the generation report (§5.4) names the re-grid.',['§3.2 (9) after (c)'],'kernel (budget owned by §12.8; milestone M4 by §16)',['§12.8 memory budget','§16 M4 measurement','§2.3 cellCm per rung'],['§5.4 generation report','§12.8'],['re-grid fallback','15.7 M cells','63 MB'])
add(I)
